            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vishnunithyasoundhar S",
                        "email": "vishnunithyasoundhar.s@intel.com",
                        "username": "VishnuNithyaSoundharS"
                    },
                    "message": "Is this an assumption or is there a reference that states this?\n\nAny NumericSensor object may or may not have a threshold irrespective of whether they are metric or value interface, right?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "I was talking about Metric.Value D-Bus interface defined in PDI. There's no threshold interface under Metric/"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vishnunithyasoundhar S",
                        "email": "vishnunithyasoundhar.s@intel.com",
                        "username": "VishnuNithyaSoundharS"
                    },
                    "message": "mmm. I understand that. Doesn't that mean we have to introduce thresholds there in PDI instead of removing it from here in PLDM?\n\nCurrently as I see, we are reusing the metric interface for some numeric sensors which are not inherently supported by redfish.\n\nBut these numeric sensors may or may not support thresholds."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes. But I'm just trying to keep the current logic in which \"updateThresholds\" is never called for a sensor that uses Metric interface (the only place it's called is in `updateReading` when useMetricInterface is false. I don't want this to go down a path where threshold interface pointers are not valid for these metric objects. We can update the logic throughout later when we actually support threshold interface for Metric objects."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vishnunithyasoundhar S",
                        "email": "vishnunithyasoundhar.s@intel.com",
                        "username": "VishnuNithyaSoundharS"
                    },
                    "message": "Agreed. We can implement the logic in future like you said on a end-to-end manner instead of the current half implemented state. Thanks for the clarification."
                }
            ],
